<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	First-party privacy manifest for the JeniFit (plankAI) app target.
	Scope: the APP's own required-reason API usage. Bundled SDKs
	(PostHog, RevenueCat, Lottie, swift-crypto, supabase-swift) ship
	their own PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy covering their usage.

	Required-reason APIs used by first-party code:
	  - UserDefaults (@AppStorage + UserDefaults.standard across 74
	    files): stores this user's own app preferences and app state
	    (onboarding answers, cohort flags, unit choice, per-day notes),
	    readable only within the app/its container. Reason CA92.1 —
	    "Access info from same app, per Apple's documentation." Not
	    tracking, not shared with third parties.

	No first-party use of file-timestamp, system-boot-time, disk-space,
	or active-keyboard required-reason APIs (audited 2026-07-04).

	NSPrivacyTracking / NSPrivacyTrackingDomains / NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes
	are intentionally omitted pending founder confirmation of the App
	Store Connect privacy answers (see 32_PRIVACY_MANIFEST.md). They must
	match the ASC nutrition label; this file declares only what is
	objectively determinable from the code.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
